# Milestone 11: reusable rules (reference/common/styles.md). Page area of 515 pt from (40, 40).
#
# For element: Block gives each Block a height of 40 and a bottom margin of 10.
# a: only the element rule.
# b: half (50 %) and tall (60), which do not clash: they add up.
# c: short and tall declare Height; short wins because it comes later in Styles, not because of the order in Style.
# d: only the tall style (60), which wins over the element rule.
# last: For id: last (20) wins over the tall style.
# e: its own Height (30) wins over all the rules.
# t: For element: Text gives Size 12, line of 14.4. For element: Block does not apply to a Text: no margin.
# p: Block with Size 20; its Text u measures 12 because the rule wins over inheritance.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 595
		Height: 842
		Margin: 40
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
		For element: Block
			Box:
				Height: 40
				Margin: 0 0 10 0
				Background: #F1EFE8
		For element: Text
			Typography:
				Size: 12
		For style: half
			Box:
				Width: 50%
		For style: tall
			Box:
				Height: 60
		For style: short
			Box:
				Height: 25
		For id: last
			Box:
				Height: 20
	Section:
		Block:
			Id: a
		Block:
			Id: b
			Style: half tall
		Block:
			Id: c
			Style: short tall
		Block:
			Id: d
			Style: tall
		Block:
			Id: last
			Style: tall
		Block:
			Id: e
			Style: tall
			Box:
				Height: 30
		Text: Texto con regla
			Id: t
		Block:
			Id: p
			Typography:
				Size: 20
			Text: Hereda
				Id: u
